entry element
term: Element
related_terms: atom
related_terms: atomic-number
related_terms: periodic-table
related_terms: isotope
related_terms: proton
quick_facts: Every atom of an element has the same number of protons
quick_facts: About 118 elements are known
quick_facts: The periodic table lists them in order of atomic number
quick_facts: Atoms of one element can differ in neutrons: those are isotopes
quick_facts: Change the number of protons and you change the element

sources:
    {"organization":"OpenStax","title":"Chemistry 2e: The Periodic Table","url":"https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/2-5-the-periodic-table"}

definition:
    A pure substance made of only one kind of atom: every atom of an element has the same number of protons. Hydrogen, carbon, oxygen and gold are elements. About 118 elements are known, and the periodic table lists them in order of atomic number.

debunking_snippet:
    “Elements are made of different kinds of stuff.” Every atom is built from the same three particles. Only the number of protons is different.
